ic ('the sidecar carries them as aggregate_tool_calls_distinct...; the message renderer reads them from there'), while also naming usage_log.format_repetition as the 'existing ... renderer, which already formats exactly these fields'. The named renderer reads the BARE keys (usage.get('tool_calls_distinct') etc., usage_log.py:326-329), not aggregate_-prefixed keys. On the budget path every primary-diagnostic key is re-prefixed aggregate_ before landing on failure_diagnostic (completion_recovery.py:545-546), so a bare-key format_repetition would find nothing under the un-prefixed names it reads. The two claims are inconsistent against the current code.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faef19310b0d5c08f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach paragraph ('the message renderer reads them from there') and AC #2","norm_id":"n52a2c1125795e6ea","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In raise_completion_workflow_failure, build the message from an un-prefixed projection of the aggregate_* keys (e.g. map aggregate_tool_calls_distinct->tool_calls_distinct before calling format_repetition), or add an aggregate-aware render path; then update AC #2 to name the exact keys the message is rendered from.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without